WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.417
(soft music)

00:00:04.869 --> 00:00:05.973
- [Narrator] This is David Deutchman.

00:00:05.973 --> 00:00:07.225
- Shh.

00:00:07.225 --> 00:00:08.569
- [Narrator] This is David Deutchman.

00:00:08.569 --> 00:00:09.541
- That's better.

00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:11.490
- [Narrator] For the last
12 years, David has held

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.054
over 1200 babies at
Scottish Rite Hospital.

00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:17.309
Hey David, when can I raise my voice?

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:19.476
- After the titles appear.

00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:25.723
- [Narrator] At Children's
Healthcare of Atlanta,

00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:28.114
you'll find David
volunteering as a baby buddy,

00:00:28.114 --> 00:00:30.131
a person that spends time holding babies

00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:31.284
who are delivered prematurely

00:00:31.284 --> 00:00:33.379
or require special medical attention.

00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:35.557
- When I first came to
work for the hospital,

00:00:35.557 --> 00:00:37.501
they gave me a little baby to hold

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:41.017
and the child life person
walked by and said,

00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:42.984
"Hey, you hold babies?

00:00:42.984 --> 00:00:44.235
“I’ve got a job for you."

00:00:44.235 --> 00:00:45.520
And I just loved it.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.933
I became nicknamed by a few
nurses as the baby whisperer.

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:51.017
Alright, buddy.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:55.100
I'd be given a baby who
was screaming and crying.

00:00:55.948 --> 00:00:59.865
You'd be amazed how
quickly they can calm down.

00:01:02.316 --> 00:01:03.603
- [Narrator] Because the
babies stay in the hospital

00:01:03.603 --> 00:01:04.889
for a long period of time,

00:01:04.889 --> 00:01:06.585
most parents can't stick around,

00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:08.730
mainly because their
maternity leave runs out

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.214
or they have other kids at home.

00:01:10.214 --> 00:01:11.718
That's where David comes in.

00:01:11.718 --> 00:01:13.458
David has gone on to hold countless babies

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.406
in the neonatal intensive care unit,

00:01:15.406 --> 00:01:17.191
providing not only companionship

00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:19.143
but other medical benefits as well.

00:01:19.143 --> 00:01:20.766
Just ask Nurse Angie.

00:01:20.766 --> 00:01:24.047
- We find that holding also
can help mitigate some pain,

00:01:24.047 --> 00:01:26.917
so when our babies have heal sticks done

00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:29.773
and they're being held,
they react so much better

00:01:29.773 --> 00:01:31.686
than when they're not held.

00:01:31.686 --> 00:01:34.258
David has done this for so long now,

00:01:34.258 --> 00:01:36.571
when he takes a baby into his arms,

00:01:36.571 --> 00:01:39.753
you can see the baby relax
because David's so relaxed.

00:01:39.753 --> 00:01:42.442
So, you feel the baby's in good hands.

00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:44.654
(peaceful music)

00:01:44.654 --> 00:01:47.936
- If you're a retiree I would say to you,

00:01:47.936 --> 00:01:50.191
“Get off your butt and do something.”

00:01:50.191 --> 00:01:52.517
Volunteer doing something,

00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:54.976
and there are a lot of
different ways of doing it;

00:01:54.976 --> 00:01:58.452
doesn't have to be in
a children's hospital.

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:01.439
I know it meant a lot to
the moms and the dads, too,

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:04.199
but what it meant for me,

00:02:04.199 --> 00:02:07.714
I really feel like I'm
the one who benefits.

00:02:07.714 --> 00:02:10.464
(peaceful music)

00:02:12.678 --> 00:02:14.845
(beeping)

